
<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Additional funding for apprentices under 25</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">If you’re recruiting an apprentice aged under 25, the government will usually fund 100% of the training costs.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">You may also be eligible for an additional £1,000 to support training costs if, at the start of their apprenticeship, the apprentice:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>is aged between 16 and 18 years (or 15 if their 16th birthday falls between the last Friday of June and 31st August) or</li>
    <li>is aged 19 to 24 and has an education, health and care (EHC) plan, or has been in the care of their local authority.</li>
</ul>
<p class="govuk-body">You can also explore receiving a transfer of levy funds from another organisation, 
    which can help cover the cost of training up to the funding band maximum for the full duration of the apprenticeship. 
    For more information, see the <a class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state" target="_blank" href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/apprenticeship-funding-rules">apprenticeship funding rules (opens in a new tab)</a>. </p>